1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Found on ship logue, [KCM Source ID R9] Kari Ruud Record:  83061 Prot. No:  14 Year:  1887 Page No: 164 Line No:  18 New Family Gr:  1 Contract Date:  20 Jul 1887 Dep Date:  21 Jul 1887 Occupation:  P. Sex:  k Age:  21 Residence: 
2 CONC  Numedal Destination:  New York Agent:  Fr. Lie Ship:  Hekla Payment:  Ppd
2 CONT
2 CONT It is believed and has been said that Carrie was in love with John's brother first and when John told her that his brother was dead, she married him.  Years later she found out that John's brother was alive and was so angry that s
2 CONC he left John and moved to Salt Lake City, Utah.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is buried under the name of Carrie Rudd Hansen at Wasatch Lawn Burial Gardens at 3401 South Highland Drive, Salt Lake City and it is believed that her name in Norway was spelled Kari. It is also believed that she changed every
2 CONC thing she could about her Norwegian heritage
2 CONT === GEDCOM Source ===
