3 STAE Utah
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The Salt Lake Tribune Sunday, November 26, 1972 page C17
2 CONT
2 CONT FRANK BRINGARD
2 CONT
2 CONT Midvale - Frank Bringard, 84, of 396 E. Center St., Midvale, died Nov. 23, 1972, at his home. Born July 6, 1888 at Breckenridge, Colo. to John and Carrie Rudd Bringard. He married Weltha Clark July 8, 1912 in Panguitch. The marria
2 CONC ge was later solemnized in the St. George Temple. She died Nov. 11, 1966. He was a former resident of Panguitch and Delta, Utah.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors: sons and daughters, Gene, Midvale; Samuel and John both of Delta; Mrs. A. T. (Norma) Heil, Reedley, Calif.; Mrs. N. L. (Irene) Wilder, San Francisco, Calif.; Mrs. Robert (Janice) Hodgen, Monterey, Calif.; Mrs. Harold (E
2 CONC valynn) Watts, Weed Heigh, Nev.; Mrs. Kelton (Donna) Peck and Mrs. Roger (Hazel) Edwards, both of Midvale; Mrs. Russle (Geneil) Bunker, South Jordan; Mrs. Pete (Dolores) Anderson, Roy; Mrs. Mary Horrocks of Kaysville; Mrs. Fred (M
2 CONC yrel) Rowley, Fillmore; 51 grandchildren; 38 great-grandchildren. Funeral Monday at 1 p.m., Midvale Third LDS Ward Chapel, 75 Olympus St., Midvale. Friends call at Goff Mortuary, 8090 S. State St. Sunday from 6-8 p.m., and Monday 
2 CONC at the church one hour prior to services. Burial in Midvale City Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Address of death was 396 E Center St in Midvale, Salt Lake co., Utah 84047 NOTE: _CLIP _UNITS INCHES _TOP 81 _BOTTOM 569 _LEFT 731 _RIGHT 122
