1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hjelmeland Gardar og folk 2 page 197 Jørmeland (8f), Årdal II page 321 Valheimsbakkane u. Nedre Valheim (58).
2 CONT
2 CONT To America ca. 1867 with 2 children.
2 CONT
2 CONT obit: “Mrs Peterson passed peacefully away Saturday morning at the home of her daughter, Mrs Ole Erickson, four miles south of Badger where she made her home.  She had reached the ago of 80 years and the cause of her death was old
2 CONC  age, as she was sick only a few hours.  The furneral took place at the Badger Lutheran Church Monday at 2:00 o’clock and was conducted by Rev Shevland.  She leaves four children to mourn her loss, Mrs Ole Erickson of Badger, Mrs.
2 CONC  Hatland of Illinois, Mr Jacob Peterson of Badger and Mr. Henry Peterson of Moreland”.
2 CONT
2 CONT came to the Fox River settlement near Leland, Ill in 1868 , when first came to USA.  was given money by the community in Årdal, after the drowing death of her husband, she came to USA with her daughter Mary and son Hans in 1868.  
2 CONC Daughter Anna and son Jakob came to USA in 1866. lived with daughter Mary Erickson near Badger, IA.
