1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Peder Andreas Hansen (1790-1849) of Log (b. 1790, Log farm, Herad parish, Farsund, Vest-Agder, Norway - d. 1849, Klungeland farm, Herad parish, Farsund, Vest-Agder, Norway) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth:
2 CONT
2 CONT Peder was the son of Hans Hansen (1749-1799) of Log; and Pernille Helene Pedersdatter (1764-after1801) of Meberg. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Baptism:
2 CONT
2 CONT He was baptised as "Peder Andreas Hansen" on January 03, 1790 at Herad, Vest-Agder, Norway. His father was listed as "Hans Hanssen".
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings:
2 CONT
2 CONT Peder had the following siblings: Anne Marie Hansdatter (1785-?); possibly Inger Hansdatter I (1793) who was baptised on February 17, 1793; Aase Lene Hansdatter (1795-?); and Inger Hansdatter II (1798-?). All living children appea
2 CONC r in the 1801 Census of Farsund, Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death of Father:
2 CONT
2 CONT After his father's death in 1799, his mother married Peder Simonsen (1772-after1801) of Espelands. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage:
2 CONT
2 CONT Peder married Maren Sophia Olsdatter (1791-1868) of Gullestad, on December 28, 1811 at Herad parish, Vest-Agder, Norway. She was listed as "Maren Sophie Olsdr" and he was listed as "Peder Andreas Hansen".
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following children: Pernille Helene Pedersdatter (1812) who died as an infant; Hans Pedersen (1814-1896) of Log, who married Anne Marie Berntsdatter (1827-1884); Anna Pedersdatter (1816-1831); Olene Andrea Pedersdatte
2 CONC r (1819-1912) who married Villum Larsen (1816-1896) and had one of their children emigrate to the United States; Ole Mathias Pedersen (1822-1914), a baker who married Thea Johanne Torstensdatter (1825-1865) and had three of his ch
2 CONC ildren emigrate to the United States; Helene Elisabeth Pedersdatter (1825-?); Peder Pedersen (1829-c1830) who died as an infant; Peder Andreas Pedersen (1831-?) who worked as a breadseller and married Serine Larsen (1840-1905) aka
2 CONC  Severina Larsdatter, and had one of their children emigrate to the United States; and Hans Elias Pedersen (1837-?). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Vest-Agder, Norway:
2 CONT
2 CONT Peder Hansen appeared in the 1801 Norway Census living with his mother and step-father. Peder and Maren sold Log farm around 1820 and moved to Klungeland farm. They sold Klungeland in 1839 to their son, Hans Pedersen of Log. Hans 
2 CONC owned it until his death, and then it was sold to a new family. Peder's wife, Maren, appeared in the 1865 Norway Census living as a widow on Klungeland farm in Herad parish, Farsund, Vest-Agder, Norway with her son Hans. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Herad Bydebok:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Peder Andreas Hansen f. 1790. Han gifta seg i 1811 med Maren Sofie Olsdtr. Gullestad. Barn: Pernille Helene 1812 (d. liten), Hans Log 1814, Anna 1816 (d. 1831), Olene Andrea 1819, Ole Mathias 1822, Helene Elisabet 1825, Peder 182
2 CONC 9 (d. liten), Peder Andreas 1831, Hans Elias 1837. De solgte garden og flytta til Klungland i 1820? åra. Peder Andreas døde der i 1849, Maren Sofie i 1868, 78 år gml."
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial:
2 CONT
2 CONT Peder died in 1849 and was most likely buried in Herad parish, Farsund, Vest-Agder, Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT Grandchildren Emigrate:
2 CONT
2 CONT His granchildren who emigrated were: Otto Olson (1858-1921), a barber who moved to Chicago, Illinois; Salmine Pedersen who married John Edward Winblad who moved to Manhattan then Jersey City, New Jersey and then died on a trip to 
2 CONC Norway; Lena Olsen who moved to Chicago, Illinois, and married Andrew Havig Jensen; Inga Pedersen who moved to Jersey City, New Jersey and married Emil August Schneider; and Mathilda Sophia Pedersen who married Hans Schultz and af
2 CONC ter his death married Martin Andreassen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Relationship:
2 CONT
2 CONT Peder Andreas Hansen (1790-1849) was the third, great-grandfather of Richard Arthur Norton (1958- ). He was the third, great-grandfather of Judith Kaye Grothe (1947- ). He was the great-grandfather of Eddie August Schneider (1911-
2 CONC 1940). He was the second great-grandfather of Adelma Tandberg Steurer (1928- ); and June Tandberg Baker (1932- ).
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT Researched and written by Richard Arthur Norton (1958- ) for Findagrave starting on January 30, 2004.
