2 CONT ** Ole Kragenes (5), Hans Christian (2)
2 CONT
2 CONT * Ole Jonsen may have been a nephew of Salve Jonsen.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Lista bygdebok "Lunde" section indicates ownership of Kraagenes as:1743 Salve Jon(a)sen Foss fra Lyngdal (g.m. enke Guri Torsdtr)
2 CONT ** Was Salve the older brother to Ole?  Not likely, given Salve's father "John Johnsen" died years before Ole was born.  However, Salve could have had a brother John who was Ole's father.
2 CONT ** Under "Grimsby", s.629 we see:
2 CONT ** Salve Jonsen fra Bjelland, far til Peder Salvesen Kraagenes, far til Gabriel Pedersen Hananger (g.1801.m. Kirsten Hansdatter (f.1775 Grimsby))
2 CONT ** https://www.geni.com/people/Salve-Jonsen-Foss-Lyngdal/6000000032721469208
2 CONT ** s.100: https://www.nb.no/items/e54e16e46d039acfdc0d7ff7d4315ef5?page=103&searchText=%22Salve%20Jonsen%22
2 CONT ** Salve died at Kraagenes in 1783, year before Ole Johnsen married and 2 years before we know Ole and Esther were then at Kraagenes.
2 CONT
2 CONT ** In Feda bygdebok, Teistedal, s.611: https://www.nb.no/items/8fa20bf609c43df7772a204b2c2c22bc?page=613&searchText=%22Salve%20Jonsen%22
2 CONT *** Aase Jonsdatter (g.m. Torkel Anensen Teistedal) hadde flere sosken:
2 CONT **** Torkild Jonsen Haue (Lista)
2 CONT **** Salve Jonsen Kraagenes (ogsaa Titland i Feda)
2 CONT **** Dordi Jonsdatter
2 CONT **** Eli Jonsdatter (g.m. Ole Pedersen Teistedal)
2 CONT **** Aasne Jonsdatter (g. til Vatland i Feda)
2 CONT **** Anna Jonsdatter (g.m. Hans Andersen Huseby)
2 CONT **** Halvsoster Torbor Jonsdatter
2 CONT **** NOTE: No mention of an Ole Jonsen...
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ** Salve Jonsen Krågenes in Lyngdal 4 bygdebok (Kvaas): https://www.nb.no/items/6fc9c1daeebd2d4a67b5ccd097c3fa03?page=0&searchText=lyngdal
2 CONT *** 2 Sonner: Peder Salvesen og Jonas Salvesen
2 CONT *** 1774: Jonas Salvesen g.m. Jamina Bjornsdtr (Bjorn Brynes datter)
2 CONT *** 1790 > b. Bryne and he owned it
2 CONT *** [NOTE: Jonas died in 1801 and had lived at Kragenes.  Though he would have been young and possibly unmarried, he could be father to Ole Jonsen Kragenes, who would then be grandson to Salve.]
2 CONT
